  "preamble": "A lateral [l] loses its lateral contact and becomes the palatal glide [j]. In Plains Cree, Proto-Algonquian *l became y throughout (*kīla 'you' > kīya). In Italian, Latin l after an initial stop or f became j (plēnus > pieno, flōrem > fiore, clāvem > chiave). Wiktionary's Zenaga descendants of Proto-Berber words show y for singleton *l.",
